      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHAMPAGNES (2) worked to find the lead and kept kicking to make it two consecutive wins last start over 1710m at this track, getting home 6 metres ahead of her rivals. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Meets a similar line up and she can figure in the finish. POPPY POPSTAR (6) could only manage to finish fifth at her latest appearance over 2180m at Stawell, a poor reflection on her short quote. This looks a sterner test than last time but on her best form she is good enough to take this out. THE ITALIAN DREAM (8) is in the mix following a fourth at her most recent appearance over 2180m at Kilmore. SHES SKY HIGH (9) is worth some thought after her last-start fourth over 2080m at Cranbourne on June 14.",
